# Rust
target/
# Cargo.lock is tracked on purpose. PDN builds applications (podnext,
# podnext-daemon, pn-gateway), not just libraries: committing the lock is what
# makes `--locked` in CI meaningful and the builds reproducible. Ignoring it
# meant every CI run resolved dependencies afresh, so a passing run could not be
# reproduced from the commit.

